==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AuthRequired  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AuthRequired.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AuthRequired removes the only constraint that pins unauthenticated operations to AuthFailure. The injection forces an unauth op with a non-AuthFailure outcome; F_PermissionEnforcement still bars Success (it needs a caller), so Alloy will pick e.g. ValidationError, which directly violates the AuthRequiredEverywhere assertion's strict equality to AuthFailure.
    expected to FAIL: AuthRequiredEverywhere, FR_001_AuthRequired
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_001_AuthRequired: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnly  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AppendOnly.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AppendOnly removes the constraint that every AuditEntry is produced by exactly one Operation. The injection forces an orphan audit row that no Operation claims, simulating either a fabricated entry or one whose originating op was deleted — exactly what append-only is supposed to prevent.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_016_AuditAppendOnly, FR_018_AuditRetention
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditAppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_AuditRetention: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_PermissionEnforcement  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_PermissionEnforcement.als
    rationale: Clearing F_PermissionEnforcement removes the role/owner check on successful operations. The injection constructs a Member-role caller who successfully deletes a task they do not own (target.team matches header so F_CrossTeamIsolation is still satisfied). That is exactly the FR-009 violation the LeastPrivilege assertion must catch.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_009_NonOwnerMemberCannotEdit
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_009_NonOwnerMemberCannotEdit: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CrossTeamIsolation  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_CrossTeamIsolation.als
    rationale: Clearing F_CrossTeamIsolation removes the constraint that a successful op's target must live in the caller's team. The injection forces a Success whose target is in another team while the caller is a legitimate member of their declared X-Team-Id team — the canonical cross-tenant leak that FR-014's byte-equivalent 404 is built to prevent.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_011_NoCrossTeamRegardlessOfRole, FR_014_ByteEquivalentNotFound
      - NoInformationLeakage: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_011_NoCrossTeamRegardlessOfRole: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_014_ByteEquivalentNotFound: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_OwnerImmutable  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_OwnerImmutable.als
    rationale: Clearing F_OwnerImmutable removes the constraint that PATCH bodies attempting to set owner_id are rejected. The injection forces a successful EditTask whose request body included an owner_id change — exactly the v1 immutability violation FR-006 must catch.
    expected to FAIL: FR_006_OwnerImmutable
      - FR_006_OwnerImmutable: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AuditCompleteness removes the constraint that every successful mutating op writes exactly one audit row. The injection forces a successful EditTask with no associated audit entry — the missing-trail half of SC-007 that AuditCompleteness must catch.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)

